<title>UK: Logica falls on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Logica falls on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Logica Plc led the technology and support services sector lower on Tuesday as investors took profits after a recent surge in share prices, dealers said.</p>
<p>Logica shares were marked down 45p to 977-1/2p, though volume was thin with only 39,211 shares changing hands.</p>
<p>Elsewhere, shares in F.I. Group fell 25p to 530, while shares Parity Plc eased 21-1/2p to 540. Shares in Sema Group fell 45p to 1367-1/2.</p>
<p>Some linked profit-taking to the recent weakness in the Nasdaq index, which is weighted heavily with technology stocks.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
